{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/6525","createdAt":"2026-10-03T08:44:01Z","decision":"accept_intent","decisionDigest":"sha256:04e4331376468086a4d05ffa2995dd38b93d08165d86240fe18175a42c175f18","decisionId":"rdec-0d19fe39512395504a16ae4e2f4df8c3","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:9e66186619980ba47dcddef809f2be9d0bc1174aa92f16755e15eed894982bf2","packageIdentity":"epkg-064f57479a01a4740491a18d7cae54f3b8b7c7de6f9ee365f3b4c549a7881198","prNumber":"6525","reason":"Agree with the intent, with one regression to fix first: inline // comments now parse, but a whole-line comment indented with a non-ASCII space now empties the whole menu file. At head 913e112d, a trailing // comment after content parses (1 row, where quattro c05d9019 drops the file), // inside a string survives, trailing commas still parse, and menu-test.sh passes (130 ok). The regression: a no-break space, U+2028, U+3000, a vertical tab or a form feed indenting a // line, or a BOM later in the file, makes the file contribute 0 rows, because JSON.parse accepts only ASCII whitespace. Copying any such character outside a string as a plain space keeps the old behaviour. #13968 fixes the same inline-comment bug (#13493), so whichever lands second needs a rebase.","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
